Well, you never know.

256
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:35,861
It could happen.

257
00:15:39,420 --> 00:15:41,020
Let's get started, Roland.

258
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,280
Time is money. But, Mr.

259
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:46,337
Kaiba, we're still waiting
for one more challenger.

260
00:15:46,420 --> 00:15:48,080
Then he's disqualified.

261
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,040
Didn't I make that clear?

262
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:52,200
Uh, yes, sir.

263
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,660
Pardon my tardiness.

264
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,197
Traffic was a nightmare.

265
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:57,580
But I rose to the occasion.

266
00:15:58,060 --> 00:16:01,260
By the way, Herr Khyber, I'm Siegfried.

267
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:05,220
I don't care who you are.

268
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:08,281
You show some respect if
you want to stick around.

269
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:14,920
May I have your attention, please?

270
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:17,157
This day will go down in history.

271
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:23,080
For today begins the most prestigious Duel
Monsters Tournament ever to be organized!

272
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:26,840
Welcome to the Kyber
Court Grand Championship!

273
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,960
Let's strut our stuff!

274
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:31,730
Right.

275
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:42,040
We've circled the globe to bring you
this all-star congregation of duelists!

276
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:47,800
First up, the new boy wonder of Dooling,
the prodigy who's yet to be defeated.

277
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:52,780
The one, the only, Leapin' Leon Wilson!

278
00:16:53,540 --> 00:16:54,370
No way!

279
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:56,697
Who knew that kid was such a big shot?

280
00:16:56,780 --> 00:17:00,251
He's a mystery, wrapped in a
riddle, wrapped in a bathroom.

281
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:02,160
Fortune Salim!

282
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:08,357
And straight from the Wild West, please
welcome the Lone Dealer, Shane Jordan!

283
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:13,440
Next, it's the Siberian
Muscle, Sergei Dimonoff!

284
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:16,597
And always clued into his
opponent's strategies,

285
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:19,880
it's the calm and collected super sleuth,

286
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,760
Detective Paul McGregor!

287
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:28,940
And of course, our very own
wild child, the Monkey Man!

288
00:17:29,580 --> 00:17:33,880
He extracts points from his opponents
with surgical precision, Dr.

289
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:34,957
Richard Gault!

290
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:41,560
Next, it's the master of the magic cards,
the always debonair, Balfree Ginger!

291
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:47,220
Zing isn't always believing,

292
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:52,060
just as the dual
illusionist, Totani Eolos!

293
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:59,720
And the thunder from down under, here
to duel and plunder, Ethan Shark!

294
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:03,737
He thinks, therefore he is Jafar Shin!

295
00:18:03,820 --> 00:18:06,337
And don't be fooled by Vivian.

296
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,500
Hey, it's her.

297
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:10,580
This delicate flower pack's quite a kick.

298
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:16,320
And of course, the youngest
regional champ, Rebecca Hawkins.

299
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:24,420
Next, it's Joey Wheeler, our
overwhelming underdog. Aw, yeah!

300
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:29,180
Hey, how about a little respect?

301
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:35,600
And hailing from parts unknown,
The Masked Duelist, Afnog Otum!

302
00:18:35,940 --> 00:18:36,800
Afnog?

303
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,560
Don't we know him?

304
00:18:38,820 --> 00:18:44,820
And our final challenger, the
always stylish Zig Green Lloyd!

305
00:18:47,160 --> 00:18:51,020
And our defending champion, Yuki Moto!

306
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:56,337
Whoever wins this 16th Duelist
Elimination Competition will go on

307
00:18:56,420 --> 00:19:00,217
to face Yuki for the International
Duel Monsters Championship Crown!

308
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:05,182
I gotta say, this looks like the toughest
bunch of competitors we ever faced, Duke.

309
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:06,540
Uh-huh, me too.

310
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:08,380
To ensure fair play,

311
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:13,168
match pairings will be randomly chosen
by our computer just before every duel.

312
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:17,237
That means you won't have a chance to
prepare for your opponents ahead of time.

313
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:18,150
Yeah,

314
00:19:18,233 --> 00:19:22,157
and it means that none of these guys will
have a chance to prepare for me either.

315
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:25,100
Once again, on behalf of
the Kaiba Corporation,

316
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,797
I'd like to wish you all the best of luck.

317
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:32,680
You represent the top-ranked
duelists from across the globe,

318
00:19:32,980 --> 00:19:35,200
but only one of you can be proud,

319
00:19:35,520 --> 00:19:37,080
the world champion!
